  "arrangerNotes": "First strain, verse 1 (12 bars), vocal line, transcribed by visual reading of the original 1914 Pace & Handy sheet music (scan and LilyPond transcription saved in scores/b9/scan/), key G major, 2/4 (durations in quarter-note beats). Blue notes replaced by the nearest drum note: the three B flats (the blue 3rd, b3, on 'sun' twice and on 'he') are played as 3 (B natural), keeping the falling 3-2-1 'sun go down'; the D sharp on the first 'de' is played as 5, (D). The printed grace note (A sharp) before 'I' is left out. Melody only: the 1914 lyrics are printed in dialect spelling, so they are left out and the tune is given without words. Range low 5 to 5. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums).",
  "verified": true
